{
  "name": "shortlisting raises a request; the email is released only on acceptance",
  "description": "ADR-0005, and the deliberate inversion of how sourcing tools normally work. Adding someone to a shortlist does NOT disclose their email — it creates a contact request the contributor must accept. Releasing contact details on the strength of one side's interest is what makes those tools feel extractive, and the whole consent model would be hollow if a shortlist click bypassed it.\n\nThe request also discloses what we know about the hirer: sam_studio's organization was verified on identity but never on payment, so the contributor is told before deciding.\n\nUpdated for RFC-0008 §3a: adding an entry stages it privately and discloses nothing. The contact request — and therefore the disclosure this case is about — is created by confirm. That moves WHEN consent is sought without changing the rule that it must be sought.\n\nREWRITTEN FOR ADR-0024. A role no longer has one `location`, an `address_id` and a list of `eligible_countries`: it holds a set of location entries — remote from anywhere, remote within a named country, or onsite at one of the organisation's addresses. The hirer reads every entry with `mode`, `country` and `address`; a contributor reads a country (or null for anywhere) and, for onsite, a city — never a street. The three old keys are gone from every request and response. Both seeded roles are remote from anywhere, so the contributor reads one entry with a null country.",
  "seed": ["principals", "catalogue", "repositories", "scored_population"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "_step": "Tiny Studio puts Alice on its job. Staging is private: no email, no notification, no contact request.",
      "as": "sam_studio",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/org-roles/{{startup.id}}/roles/{{startup.role}}/candidates",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "{{alice.id}}",
          "note": "Strong retry-semantics work."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "_note": "No email in the response, and none is released: that is what accepting a contact request does (ADR-0008 §3a).",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
          "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
          "github_login": "<string>",
          "note": "Strong retry-semantics work.",
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c003",
            "username": "sam",
            "display_name": "Sam Ortega",
            "active": true
          },
          "added_at": "<timestamp>",
          "notified_at": null,
          "contact_status": "",
          "accepted": false
        },
        "db": {
          "contact_requests": {
            "_note": "Zero. Staging is private — RFC-0008 §3a.",
            "where": {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
